put it, and both files are here exactly as shipped.

  stb_truetype.h  v1.26
  stb_image.h     v2.30, from nothings/stb commit
                  013ac3beddff3dbffafd5177e7972067cd2b5083,
                  sha256 594c2fe35d49488b4382dbfaec8f98366defca819d916ac95becf3e75f4200b3
  stb_image_write.h  v1.16, from the same commit,
                  sha256 cbd5f0ad7a9cf4468affb36354a1d2338034f2c12473cf1a8e32053cb6914a05

This note exists because the rule in CLAUDE.md is that anything vendored
records its licence beside it. For stb the licence travels inside the file,
so this is a pointer rather than a copy: if the two ever disagree, the text
in stb_truetype.h is the one that counts.

stb_impl.c is not upstream. It is the one translation unit that defines
STB_TRUETYPE_IMPLEMENTATION, STB_IMAGE_IMPLEMENTATION and
STB_IMAGE_WRITE_IMPLEMENTATION, written here, and it carries no separate
terms beyond the above.
